**Bootstrap reorder (scripts/windows11/windows11_bootstrap.ps1)**
- Round 48's guest-driver-vs-2100780.diff holds the earlier version. The only changes since then are:
  - the hive and powercfg block now sits after Register-ScheduledTask and before the Startup folder and JappFixture.cmd;
  - the [GC]::Collect line and its comment are gone;
  - one new comment explains the order.
- Every command and argument is otherwise byte-identical, so the bootstrap still does everything it did: seed copy, attestor file, SYSTEM AtLogOn task, Default-profile load/add/add/unload, powercfg, Startup folder and entry.
- The order is valid. Nothing depends on anything else here: the hive bracket, powercfg, the task registration and the Startup-folder write are independent.
- Removing [GC]::Collect is safe. Only reg.exe child processes touch the loaded hive, so PowerShell itself holds no handle into it.
- With ErrorActionPreference Stop, every throw comes before the JappFixture.cmd Set-Content, and that write is the file's last statement.
- windows11_deployment.py has no other guest launcher (no FirstLogonCommands), so a failure in any first-logon step leaves no guest startup entry. Only the attestor task stays registered, which is harmless.
- The guest.ps1 comment's numbers match the retained diag-serial-writes files:
  - rounds 39/40 environment writes: 70, 44, 49, 43 and 63 ms, so 43 to 70 ms over five VMs;
  - rounds 45/47 keyboard writes: 264, 224, 197, 287 and 228 ms, so 197 to 287 ms over five VMs, at about 10.84 to 10.87 K characters;
  - extrapolating the rounds 39/40 rate to the keyboard receipt gives about 0.47 to 0.77 s, matching "about 0.5 to 0.8 s".

